    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The responses of the system correspond to 1DOF oscillators and using a least square estimation we obtained the values of the mechanical parameters. Those values are given in Table 1 with respect to the parameters given by the manufacturer."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 106,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 55.667, 234.223, 160.333, 248.223 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "3.3 Modal parameters"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 108,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 55.333, 167.89, 288.333, 228.223 ],
    "font" : "Arial-BoldMT",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The developed method requires an external possibility of making the shaker vibrate and is quite difficult to apply to larger shakers. In this case, modal analysis is an alternative since the mechanical parameters and the modal ones are equivalent to characterize the system. In this section, a short review of the modal theory"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
